WEBVTT

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.700
The Texas Raiders lose consecutively!

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.570
They were unable to get any closer to winning the championship today.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.900
Oh, man. What are those guys doing?

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.780
Hey, Junior!

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:19.750
The coach is calling for you!

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.420
I'm being called up!?

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:25.750
That's right.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.310
The original plan was...

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.160
to call you up to the Majors after the Minors season ended,

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.380
but it seems that the Raiders' third baseman has been put on the disabled list.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.220
Well, it'll be tough for us to lose you,

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.720
but if the upper guys have an emergency, there's not much we can do.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.880
You're on the first flight to Texas tomorrow morning.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:43.770
Wait a minute!

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.360
These playoffs...

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.440
Since we lost the first game, we're behind!

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.830
I can't just abandon the team for the Majors.

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:53.110
It's an order from the top. You have no say in it.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:58.070
I know you were anticipating your duel with that Japanese pitcher,

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:01.180
but he injured his hand during today's match.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.200
He won't be pitching for the rest of the series,

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.200
got it?

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:51.560
Old man!

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.360
Oh, Shigeno!

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.040
How's your hand?

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.970
They said my bones are fine,

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.360
so I'll be able to pitch again in a few days.

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.730
You... You're planning to pitch?

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:03.210
Naturally.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.550
The Bats' first victory is on the line.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.500
You think I can sit out with just a minor injury?

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:10.910
Plus,

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.630
my duel with him...

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:16.350
isn't over yet.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.030
Don't be stupid!

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:22.390
You <i>injured</i> your left hand, you know!

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:26.290
Your real challenge will come in the Majors!

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.280
What in the world are you thinking?

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.370
The Texas Raiders' situation remains the same.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.580
Replacing Maurice, the third baseman who was injured today,

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.670
will be a player from their Triple A team, the Oklahoma Falcons.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.610
They've decided to bring in Joe Gibson Jr. as an emergency backup.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:45.570
Gibson Jr. is the son of the Titans' ace, Joe Gibson,

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.580
and he's also the number one rookie from the American draft.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.830
He's had a .382 batting average this season,

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.370
made 48 home runs,

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.830
and he's been a major part of the Falcons' regional victory,

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.090
so the Raiders brass are expecting great things from him.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:12.940
Out!

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:16.960
Gibson Jr. ruins yet another chance.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:20.900
He has yet to make a hit since entering the Majors.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.260
Maybe this is what they call the Majors baptism?

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.050
The Raiders have lost five straight games now.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:29.070
They still need three more wins to take the championship.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.670
And you call yourself Gibson's son!?

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.870
Are you listening!? Look at the ball!

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.790
Quit!

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:46.930
Geez, this is the number one draft rookie?

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.080
I know people can't always live up to their reputations, but this?

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:52.330
Maybe you came to the Majors too soon.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:57.080
Hey.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.500
Jackson.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.800
Don't let it get to you.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.820
Almost no one plays great right away.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:10.450
Also, as a great rookie with a father like yours, of course there's a lot of pressure on you.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.790
But your hitting isn't bad.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:17.610
If you just relax and concentrate on batting, you'll see results in no time.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.290
See ya, rookie.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:30.550
Now for the results of the third match of the Triple A Championship, held today.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.420
The teams each had one win before this match.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:37.340
Both starting pitchers, Bats' Shiba and Falcons' Albina, pitched strongly,{"shiibaa" and "arubina"}

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:39.230
and the score was even at zero until the middle of the game.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:42.280
The equilibrium was broken in the 7th inning,

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:45.220
as the Bats got a headstart with Sanders' two runs.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.920
The Falcons managed to take one point back in the bottom of the 8th,

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:50.630
and had a great chance with one out and the bases loaded.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:56.490
The Bats surprisingly sent out their closer, Shigeno, who had been out with an injured left hand.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.670
Shigeno managed to shut out the rest of the batters,

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.420
and the Bats won the match 2-1.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:06.090
The Bats are now ahead 2-1...{I can't hear the next part of this, because Junior thinks too loud. But it's probably not important, since he is deafening it with his thoughts.}

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.090
<i>I see.</i>

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.140
<i>So he really wasn't...</i>

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:10.920
<i>the type of person who would sit out after something like that!</i>

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:25.400
Now hitting, number 4: Joe Gibson Jr!

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.420
Bring in a pinch hitter!

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:30.700
This rookie can't hit anything! He can't be expected to do anything!

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.700
Go back and train in Triple A!

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:52.250
Well done, Junior! Headstart home run!

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.300
I've waited for this, Junior!

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.450
<i>If we just win a few,</i>

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.600
<i>the rest of the matches won't be important.</i>

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.600
<i>In that case, let's just hurry and win this!</i>

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.580
<i>Just you wait, Honda Jr!</i>

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:06.630
<i>Even if I have to go back to the Minors,</i>

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:08.780
<i>I'll have my revenge!</i>

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:16.790
His second home run today...

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.460
Plus, in two matches in a row...

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:38.470
Safe!

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:43.400
Damn it!

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:48.220
Boss, we have to use Shigeno here!

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:50.960
We've lost three games, it'll all be over if we lose this one!

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:54.870
Pitcher, Shigeno!

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:03.950
Him again...

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.790
A troublesome guy has appeared on the field...

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.300
You know, Shigeno?

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:09.250
You're not in peak condition yet,

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.260
so take it easy.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:14.590
But I know it's useless to tell you that.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:18.050
You know it by now, old man!

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:20.100
Let's hurry up and finish this!

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:21.930
Yeah!

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:24.100
Play!

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:28.690
Strike!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.270
Strike out!

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.750
Game over!

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.440
We did it!

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.880
Now we're 3-3!

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:53.150
If we just win tomorrow, we'll take the championship!

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.230
Out!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.690
Out!

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:15.570
They did it! The Raiders win!

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:19.490
They've won the regional championship!

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.770
Hey, Gibson!

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.200
What are you doing at a time like this?

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:49.970
Come on, hurry up!

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:52.870
I'm sorry, Jackson. There's something I have to do.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:53.730
Something you have to do?

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:56.200
Wait a minute! What do you mean?

00:09:56.570 --> 00:10:00.400
You have something more important to do than celebrate with your teammates!?

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.180
I still have things to take care of in the Minors.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:09.690
Tell the coach that I'll be missing tomorrow's game.

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.340
I'll be back the day after.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:25.370
Clink! He hits it,

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:28.690
but it's a grounder straight to second, and it's a double play!

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:33.440
Sanders has no hits in four at-bats in this crucial game. He's holding his team back!

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:36.780
Hey, don't jinx me!

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:39.560
Tomorrow, my son is coming in from Boston.

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:42.120
I can't let him see a bad performance.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:49.000
We won't lose.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.670
We'll definitely win tomorrow and take the championship,

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:53.090
with you and I both...

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.690
playing big roles in the match.

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:58.510
Yeah.

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:00.930
We'll definitely win!

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:12.270
Why is he here?

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:16.690
Oh yeah, I heard that the Raiders won the regional championship yesterday.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:21.160
So he came back down to the Minors just to play against us?

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.480
<i>What's the meaning of this?</i>

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:26.220
<i>Are you that obsessed with beating us?</i>

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:30.290
<i>Don't worry,</i>

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.800
<i>I'll just take you down instead!</i>

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.170
Play ball!

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:40.090
Now, at last, it's the final game of the season.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:46.600
The Bats and the Falcons each have three wins, and the deciding match is underway!

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:52.470
Who will win this match and seize the glorious championship trophy?

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:56.830
Are there any tickets left?

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:57.660
Huh?

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:58.780
No, no.

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.750
You can't get in by coming this late.

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:02.620
There isn't even standing room left.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:04.040
I see.

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:05.520
In that case, sorry,

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:08.060
but could you please call your manager?

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:09.040
Huh?

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.240
Calling my manager, what do you think...

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:16.140
Y-You!

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:21.970
This is a free fansub.

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:21.970
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:30.770
Now hitting, number 1: Joe Gibson Jr!

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.930
Junior! We're counting on you!

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.730
Hit a big one!

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.610
<i>No outs, and a runner on first,</i>

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.650
<i>but we can't get ahead of ourselves.</i>

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:48.780
<i>At worst, we'll walk him.</i>

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:52.200
<i>Not enough!</i>

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.830
He did it!

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:06.890
A two-run home run!

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.300
<i>Hurry up and disappear.</i>

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:12.270
<i>My fight isn't with you.</i>

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.440
I hate this!

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:21.230
I hate this!

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.400
I guess I'll get warmed up.

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:25.780
Hey, Shigeno!

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:29.910
I'm counting on you to give me the sign before the match is out of reach, Boss.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:41.890
He did it, Mr. Gibson.

00:13:41.890 --> 00:13:44.340
Your son made an excellent home run.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:51.110
But still, to have a big star like you here in a Minor League stadium makes me very proud.

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:52.980
Also, your son...

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:55.850
showed great results to you right away.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:58.480
He's got enough skill to be a star for sure.

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:07.330
<i>You've grown,</i>

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.070
<i>Honda Goro.</i>

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:15.200
Hey, Gibson!

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:16.960
I've been told that your father...

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.040
is in the box seats.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:23.070
Strike out!

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.100
<i>Why is my old man here?</i>

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:37.690
<i>He's never come...</i>

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:40.460
<i>to see any of my games.</i>

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:41.940
<i>Why would he come to this one?</i>

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.490
<i>It's him!</i>

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:48.420
<i>There's no mistake!</i>

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:50.600
<i>My old man didn't come to see me.</i>

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.280
<i>He came for him!</i>

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:53.950
<i>To watch the son of Honda Shigeharu,</i>

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:56.370
<i>who tore our family apart!</i>

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:00.090
<i>Sorry.</i>

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:03.000
<i>I have to pitch here, in Japan.</i>

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:08.030
<i>For the Japanese fans, and for Honda Jr's sake.</i>

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:14.120
Out!

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:17.870
<i>Since then,</i>

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:20.690
<i>my old man has never looked at me.</i>

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:23.940
<i>My father upheld his baseball career because of...</i>

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:27.860
<i>the heavy cross he had to carry after killing Honda Shigeharu,</i>

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:31.280
<i>and to guide and watch over Honda's son,</i>

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.180
<i>and only him!</i>

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.050
Mr. Gibson.

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:44.360
The preparations for the VIP room are complete, so please follow me.

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:46.090
Thanks.

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:55.300
Junior.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:00.370
It's been a long time, Father.

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:03.490
Did you see my splendid home run?

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:07.890
Sorry, but could you give us a minute?

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:09.270
Yes, sir.

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.700
I'll wait by the VIP room.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.140
Yeah, I saw it.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:19.310
It was a high ball that was clearly a bad pitch.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:21.320
To someone like you, who is already in the Major Leagues,

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:22.710
it was an easy ball to hit.

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:26.120
Well, of course...

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:29.830
Of course you wouldn't care about what I'm doing at this point.

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:31.660
The one you came here to watch today...

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:33.260
was not me, your son, but rather...

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.930
the only child...

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:38.310
of the Japanese player you killed, right?

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:41.520
That's right.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.670
While touring in Saint Louis with the Titans,

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:47.290
I thought I'd stretch my legs and see how Goro's doing.

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:48.460
Naturally,

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:50.330
I've watched over him and his actions...

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:52.700
ever since he came to America.

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:56.210
I'm obligated to watch over him, after all.

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:57.680
Is there a problem with that?

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.380
I see.

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:05.410
I guess you're pleased, then,

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:08.860
seeing your favorite come all the way here.

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:10.920
But...

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:13.920
I'm not going to let things go your way.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:16.100
We made a bet, you see.

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:19.040
If I hit a home run off his pitch,

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:21.350
he'll leave America!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.160
Be sure to watch carefully...

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:27.030
as your treasured favorite gets beaten down by me,

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:29.900
and has to give up his dream of being in the Majors!

00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:38.660
You can't hit Goro's pitch.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:42.240
What!?

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.950
I'll say it again:

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:46.630
You're not good enough to hit Goro's pitches yet.

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:47.670
Not physically,

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:50.340
and not mentally.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:55.510
You're saying that I can't hit his pitch? You bastard!

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:58.260
Is it that fun...

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:59.520
to favor him over your own son?

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:00.730
It's not favoritism.

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:02.180
It's just the unbiased truth.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:03.600
Also,

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:07.210
I know you don't think of me as your father, and that's your right,

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:10.360
but to me, I have only one son.

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:13.530
Instead of wasting your time being jealous,

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:18.670
you should plan out how you'll hit Goro's pitch.

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:20.690
Even if he's pitching at 100 mph,

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:23.450
to be struck out without even grazing a single pitch is disgraceful.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.460
Ever since Little League,

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:28.750
you've been excellent against fastballs when batting in the left batter's box.

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.380
Little League?

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:32.430
What do you mean by that?

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:34.090
You never saw any of my games!

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:36.010
Just watch!

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:37.630
I'll banish him...

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:38.760
from this country!

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:48.640
Ball!

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:52.520
Boss!

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:55.510
I-I'm counting on you, Shiba!

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:57.830
Just hold out for one more inning!

00:18:57.830 --> 00:18:59.030
Do your best!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:01.610
Ball!

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:02.410
Ball four!

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.050
Boss!

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:09.060
Shiba is at his limit!

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:11.450
Plus, if we let them get any further ahead...

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.800
Pitcher, Shigeno!

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:22.260
Finally it's my turn. I'm tired of waiting.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:24.320
Finally!

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:26.070
Go, Goro!

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:28.230
Crush those lousy Falcons!

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:32.310
Huh?

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:35.490
That's some great booing...

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:39.530
Well, the Falcons have been completely shut out by Shigeno, after all.

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:43.220
We're counting on you, Shigeno.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:45.030
You're our last hope.

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:47.640
Leave it to me.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:49.720
It's only the fourth inning, a third of the way through the match.{Kohn: I think that's what he means by "a third", but not sure.}

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:53.210
I'll blow this booing away at full speed!

00:19:53.540 --> 00:20:00.090
Now hitting, number 1: Joe Gibson Jr!

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:13.270
<i>I'll say it again:</i>

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.740
<i>You're not good enough to hit Goro's pitches yet.</i>

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:18.160
<i>Not physically,</i>

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:19.360
<i>and not mentally.</i>

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:21.620
<i>Come on.</i>

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:23.740
<i>Your 100 mph fastball...</i>

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.450
<i>I'll beat it!</i>

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:34.800
<i>Shigeno, I know you're focused on your duel with him,</i>

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:38.170
<i>but right now we have to make sure we put him down!</i>

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:44.640
Strike!

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:46.350
<i>All right!</i>

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:51.350
Strike two!{Synmais: "Strike two!"}

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:54.020
<i>Okay, we've cornered him!</i>

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:59.730
<i>Both of those were controlled 90 mph pitches...</i>

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:04.750
<i>Shigeno.</i>

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:06.350
<i>Now go for the inside corner.</i>

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:08.160
<i>We'll get him with this one!{Not sure about this line}</i>

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:13.580
Foul!

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:16.300
<i>We're saved...</i>

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.760
<i>Why?</i>

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:22.920
<i>Why aren't you throwing </i>that<i> pitch?</i>

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:24.720
<i>That 100 mph pitch...</i>

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:26.840
<i>that struck me out!</i>

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:33.060
Foul!

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:40.180
<i>It can't be that he...</i>

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:41.640
<i>made a foul on purpose.</i>

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:45.180
<i>I don't know what you're trying to do,</i>

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:48.040
<i>but right now it's just important
that you don't throw a wild pitch.</i>

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:53.000
<i>Don't you understand yet?</i>

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:54.080
<i>You can't bring me down...</i>

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:57.120
<i>with this kind of pitch!</i>

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:08.990
Out!

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:14.860
You did it!

00:22:14.860 --> 00:22:16.560
Of course!

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:20.310
But it was a perfect hit!

00:22:21.530 --> 00:22:22.730
We're saved!

00:22:27.910 --> 00:22:28.970
Nice catch!

00:22:28.970 --> 00:22:30.370
Yeah...

00:24:12.010 --> 00:24:14.720
The match against the Falcons with the championship on the line...

00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:15.970
is finally coming to an end!

00:24:16.920 --> 00:24:18.890
Gibson, please watch...

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:20.350
my growth!

00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:23.650
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.650 --> 00:24:24.650
A Real Rival.

00:24:25.730 --> 00:24:28.220
Run towards the stage of your dreams!
